1
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:10,940
A round pizza is cut from the centre into 4 slices.

2
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:18,350
Three of the slices have angles of 95 degrees, 120 degrees and 80 degrees at the centre.

3
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,770
What angle does the last slice make?

4
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:24,330
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:27,680
All the way round the centre is one full turn.

6
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:30,200
A full turn is 360 degrees.

7
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:34,550
The three slices we know add up to 295 degrees.

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,490
360 minus 295 is 65.

9
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:41,130
The last slice has an angle of 65 degrees.

10
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:45,470
Remember: angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees.

11
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,510
That is half a turn.

12
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:55,290
If one angle is 128 degrees, the other is 180 minus 128, which is 52 degrees.

13
00:00:55,340 --> 00:01:00,170
The angles around a point always add up to 360 degrees.

14
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:04,670
Here, two of the angles are 140 degrees and 85 degrees.

15
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:06,290
Find angle b.

16
00:01:06,340 --> 00:01:08,790
140 plus 85 is 225.

17
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,560
360 minus 225 is 135.

18
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:14,740
So b is 135 degrees.

19
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:15,520
Your turn.

20
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:20,370
Three angles around a point are 200 degrees, 95 degrees, and y.

21
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:20,910
Find y.

22
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:24,400
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:26,810
200 plus 95 is 295.

24
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:29,360
360 minus 295 is 65.

25
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:32,330
So y is 65 degrees.

26
00:01:32,380 --> 00:01:35,860
A quadrilateral is a shape with 4 straight sides.

27
00:01:35,910 --> 00:01:39,870
Draw a diagonal, and it splits into 2 triangles.

28
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:43,950
The angles in each triangle add up to 180 degrees.

29
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,780
So the angles in a quadrilateral add up to 2 times 180, which is 360 degrees.

30
00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:55,280
In this one, 74 plus 106 plus 82 is 262.

31
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:57,530
360 minus 262 is 98.

32
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:00,890
So angle d is 98 degrees.

33
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:02,540
Here is the method.

34
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:05,410
Step 1: decide which fact to use.

35
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,410
A straight line is 180.

36
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,320
Around a point is 360.

37
00:02:09,370 --> 00:02:10,880
A triangle is 180.

38
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:13,430
A quadrilateral is 360.

39
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,350
Step 2: add the angles you know.

40
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,270
Step 3: subtract from the total.

41
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:24,190
Step 4: check that your answer looks sensible on the diagram.

42
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,490
Five equal angles meet at a point.

43
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,400
How big is each one?

44
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,670
The total is 360 degrees.

45
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,410
Share it equally: 360 divided by 5 is 72.

46
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:37,230
Each angle is 72 degrees.

47
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:42,870
Around a point, the angles are 2 x, 3 x, 100 degrees and 80 degrees.

48
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,010
Find x.

49
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:46,020
They add up to 360.

50
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:50,920
2 x plus 3 x plus 100 plus 80 equals 360.

51
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:55,530
Collect like terms: 5 x plus 180 equals 360.

52
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:59,130
Subtract 180: 5 x equals 180.

53
00:02:59,180 --> 00:03:00,260
Divide by 5.

54
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:01,940
x equals 36.

55
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:02,640
Your turn.

56
00:03:02,690 --> 00:03:05,370
A quadrilateral has three right angles.

57
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:07,120
What is the fourth angle?

58
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:10,060
Pause and work it out.

59
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:14,390
Three right angles make 3 times 90, which is 270.

60
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,150
360 minus 270 is 90.

61
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,510
The fourth angle is a right angle too.

62
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,270
The shape is a rectangle.

63
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:27,550
What is the smaller angle between the hands of a clock at 4 o'clock?

64
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:30,860
The 12 hour marks share 360 degrees.

65
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:36,820
360 divided by 12 is 30 degrees between each pair of marks.

66
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:39,320
From 12 to 4 is 4 marks.

67
00:03:39,370 --> 00:03:41,200
4 times 30 is 120.

68
00:03:41,250 --> 00:03:44,360
The angle is 120 degrees.

69
00:03:44,410 --> 00:03:49,210
Three angles around a point are 150 degrees, 90 degrees, and a.

70
00:03:49,260 --> 00:03:50,900
Here is Leo's working.

71
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:53,610
Which line goes wrong first?

72
00:03:53,660 --> 00:03:54,910
Line 2 is wrong.

73
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:59,240
Angles around a point add up to 360 degrees, not 180.

74
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:02,400
And an angle cannot be negative.

75
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:05,010
360 minus 240 is 120.

76
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:08,050
So a is 120 degrees.

77
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:11,220
Why are there 360 degrees in a full turn?

78
00:04:11,270 --> 00:04:16,790
The idea is thought to come from ancient Babylon, about 4,000 years ago.

79
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:20,050
The Babylonians counted in sixties.

80
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:22,580
360 is a very handy number.

81
00:04:22,630 --> 00:04:28,750
It can be divided exactly by 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10 and 12.

82
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,350
Skateboarders use the same number.

83
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:34,880
A full spin in the air is called a 360.

84
00:04:34,930 --> 00:04:36,140
One last question.

85
00:04:36,190 --> 00:04:38,320
6 equal angles meet at a point.

86
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:39,720
How big is each one?

87
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:43,020
Pause the video and answer.

88
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:45,360
360 divided by 6 is 60.

89
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:48,470
Each angle is 60 degrees.

90
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:53,500
To remember: angles around a point add up to 360 degrees.

91
00:04:53,550 --> 00:05:00,400
Angles in a quadrilateral add up to 360 degrees, because it is made of 2 triangles.

92
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:06,020
Angles on a straight line, and in a triangle, add up to 180 degrees.

93
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:10,680
Add the angles you know, subtract from the total, then check.

94
00:05:10,730 --> 00:05:15,870
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.1 on Camday.
